      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would prefer not, I dislike extra indirection of this kind. I find that it forces the reader to look up the definition and when the definition is trivial (`String`), then I haven\u0027t really gained anything from the indirection.\n\nWe already have this in the AST: it has\n\n```rust\npub type SourceDatabase \u003d files::SimpleFiles\u003cString, String\u003e;\n```\n\nbut when I jump from `sources.get(grammar.file)` to the definition of the `get` method, then I see\n\n```rust\n    pub fn get(\u0026self, file_id: usize) -\u003e Result\u003c\u0026SimpleFile\u003cName, Source\u003e, Error\u003e {\n```\n\nThis is a bit confusing: I went from a type without type parameters and end up in a place with type parameters. I start wondering what the `Name` and `Source` types are... turns out that they\u0027re `String` and `String` 😄",
